[h1]Crossover Platforms[/h1]
Space platform pieces where two paths cross straight through each other, instead of one detouring over the other.

[h2]Three crossings[/h2]
They appear together in a [b]Crossings[/b] group in the platform toolbar:
[list]
[*][b]Belt Crossing[/b] - two space belts crossing
[*][b]Belt / Pipe Crossing[/b] - a space belt crossing a space pipe
[*][b]Pipe Crossing[/b] - two space pipes crossing
[/list]
Each is a single chunk, straight across. The two paths never interact: shapes and fluids stay on the path they entered on, and a belt end can never connect to a pipe end.

[h2]Laid down by dragging, not by hand[/h2]
Drag a space belt or space pipe across one that is already there and you get a crossing in place, rather than the lift-up, across and back-down detour the game builds today.
The flip key (F by default) swaps which way the crossing's second path runs.

Two segments meeting head-on on the same axis, and anything that is not a plain straight piece - a turn, a splitter, an existing crossing - are left to the usual lift.

[h2]The game's own speeds[/h2]
A crossing is two complete space paths sharing one chunk, with nothing shared between them.
Lane counts and speeds are read from the vanilla space belt and space pipe at runtime, so belt and pipe speed research applies to a crossing exactly as it does to the track either side of it.
Select one and its side panel reports each of the two paths separately, using the game's own throughput readouts.

[h2]Before you install[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]This mod affects save games.[/b] It cannot be added to, or removed from, a save that already exists - start a new one.
[*]Available from the first milestone. Anyone installing a crossing mod is not a first-time player, and is installing it precisely to stop building lift detours, so gating it behind late research would defeat the point.
[*]Requires Shapez Shifter.
[/list]

[h2]About the art[/h2]
A crossing is drawn as two of the game's own track segments laid across each other. It reads as track rather than as a black slab, but there is no junction detail and the two decks sit level rather than one passing over the other. A purpose-built model is the obvious next step.

